{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01P47wD7bnyiYmafmN1BJHAn","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/_dev/GLB/stepwise-fifa-qa/.coda/skills/analyze-test-cases/references/phase-b-quality-analysis.md\" lines=\"126\" start=\"1\" end=\"126\" returned=\"126\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Phase B: Quality Analysis & Classification\n     2|\n     3|## Context Contract\n     4|- **Inputs:** TC_CONTEXT (from Phase A), `test_cases_path` (re-read from disk), `test_strategy_path` (re-read from disk)\n     5|- **Outputs:** Per-TC quality assessments, feasibility ratings, complexity classifications, inventory classifications\n     6|- **Carries Forward:** TC_CONTEXT updated with per-TC assessments, aggregated metrics\n     7|- **Flush After:** Raw TC content, raw strategy content, per-TC analysis text\n     8|- **Dependency:** Phase A must be COMPLETE\n     9|\n    10|---\n    11|\n    12|## Mode-Specific Behavior\n    13|\n    14|- **REPAIR:** Parse REPAIR_DIRECTIVES for targets matching TC IDs or `\"quality-analysis\"` or `\"global\"`.\n    15|  - If no directives target this phase → SKIP (preserve existing assessments).\n    16|  - If specific TC IDs targeted → re-analyze ONLY those TCs. Preserve all others verbatim.\n    17|  - If `\"global\"` → re-analyze all TCs.\n    18|- **BUILD:** Execute fully.\n    19|\n    20|---\n    21|\n    22|## Phase B Instructions\n    23|\n    24|### B.0: Mandatory Source Loading\n    25|\n    26|**CRITICAL:** After Phase A's flush, the agent knows NOTHING about the test cases.\n    27|You MUST re-read the source files before generating any analysis.\n    28|\n    29|```\n    30|READ test_cases_path   -> TC_CONTENT\n    31|READ test_strategy_path -> STRATEGY_CONTENT\n    32|READ _progress.json -> restore TC_CONTEXT\n    33|```\n    34|\n    35|**Zero Invention Checkpoint:** Verify TC_CONTENT and STRATEGY_CONTENT are in context.\n    36|If either is empty → STOP. Do NOT generate from memory or training data.\n    37|\n    38|### B.1: Analyze Provided Test Cases\n    39|\n    40|FOR EACH test case in TC_CONTEXT.test_cases (process ALL, do NOT stop early):\n    41|\n    42|1. **Load** the specific TC's full text from TC_CONTENT (match by TC ID)\n    43|2. **Assess** against quality criteria:\n    44|   - **Scenario clarity and specificity** — Are steps unambiguous? (score 1-10)\n    45|   - **Validation points defined** — Are expected results explicit? (status: defined | missing)\n    46|   - **Test data requirements specified** — Are inputs/data documented? (status: specified | needs_definition)\n    47|   - **Edge cases considered** — Does the TC cover boundary conditions? (yes | partial | no)\n    48|   - **Negative scenarios included** — Does the TC cover failure paths? (yes | partial | no)\n    49|   - **Completeness score** — Overall quality 1-10 with justification\n    50|   - **source:** TC ID from source file\n    51|3. **Rate** automation feasibility:\n    52|   - `automatable` — Can be fully automated with browser/API automation capabilities\n    53|   - `partial` — Some steps require manual intervention or visual verification\n    54|   - `manual_only` — Requires human judgment, physical interaction, or subjective assessment\n    55|   - **status:** complete | assumption (if insufficient info to determine)\n    56|4. **Classify** complexity:\n    57|   - `simple` — Single page, linear flow, ≤5 steps, basic assertions\n    58|   - `medium` — Multi-page, conditional logic, 6-15 steps, data-driven\n    59|   - `complex` — Multi-system, async operations, >15 steps, state management\n    60|   - **status:** complete | assumption\n    61|\n    62|5. **Update** TC_CONTEXT.test_cases[TC] with assessment results\n    63|6. **Update** aggregated metrics\n    64|\n    65|**IMPORTANT:** Use capability language, not tool-specific names.\n    66|Say \"browser automation\" not \"Playwright\". Say \"API testing\" not \"Postman\".\n    67|\n    68|### B.2: Classify Incoming Test Cases — Inventory-Aware\n    69|\n    70|**SKIP this step if `INVENTORY_CONTEXT.inventory_exists == false`.**\n    71|\n    72|IF `INVENTORY_CONTEXT.inventory_exists == true`:\n    73|\n    74|```\n    75|READ existing inventory from {automation_code_path}/test-inventory.md\n    76|\n    77|FOR EACH test case in TC_CONTEXT.test_cases:\n    78|  MATCH by TC ID against the existing inventory:\n    79|\n    80|  IF TC ID matches AND title + steps + assertions are functionally identical:\n    81|    classification = \"duplicate\"\n    82|    action = \"Skip — no automation changes needed\"\n    83|    status: complete\n    84|    source: inventory match at {TC ID}\n    85|\n    86|  ELSE IF TC ID matches BUT title, steps, or assertions differ:\n    87|    classification = \"update\"\n    88|    changed_fields = list of fields that differ\n    89|    action = \"Modify — existing test code must be updated\"\n    90|    status: complete\n    91|    source: inventory delta at {TC ID}\n    92|\n    93|  ELSE IF TC ID has no match:\n    94|    classification = \"new\"\n    95|    action = \"Add — new test code must be generated\"\n    96|    status: complete\n    97|    source: no inventory match\n    98|\n    99|  ADDITIONALLY:\n   100|    IF TC ID not in inventory BUT title+assertions match another TC:\n   101|      Flag as \"potential_duplicate\"\n   102|      Log warning: \"TC-XXX: Potential duplicate of TC-YYY\"\n   103|\n   104|  UPDATE TC_CONTEXT.test_cases[TC] with classification\n   105|  UPDATE metrics: increment new/update/duplicate counters\n   106|```\n   107|\n   108|---\n   109|\n   110|## Source Fidelity Check (before completing phase)\n   111|\n   112|Scan all generated assessments for:\n   113|- References to TC IDs not present in TC_CONTEXT.test_cases (hallucinated IDs)\n   114|- Feasibility ratings without justification\n   115|- Complexity ratings that contradict the step count\n   116|- Summary counts that don't match actual items\n   117|- Technology-specific language (should be capability language)\n   118|\n   119|IF violations found → correct before marking phase complete. Log corrections.\n   120|\n   121|## Post-Section Protocol\n   122|1. **Update** _progress.json with phase B completion and all metrics.\n   123|2. **Flush** TC_CONTENT, STRATEGY_CONTENT, and per-TC analysis text from memory.\n   124|3. **Verify** `_progress.json` exists and is non-empty.\n   125|4. **Log:** `\"Phase B complete. {N} TCs analyzed. Automatable: {auto}, Partial: {partial}, Manual: {manual}. Complexity: S={simple}, M={medium}, C={complex}.\"`\n   126|\n</file>","isError":false}}
