{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01KuDwh35Jur6ZemkKVT6zRi","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/_dev/GLB/stepwise-fifa-qa/.coda/skills/analyze-test-cases/references/phase-c-document-generation.md\" lines=\"225\" start=\"1\" end=\"225\" returned=\"225\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Phase C: Spec Generation & Consolidation\n     2|\n     3|## Context Contract\n     4|- **Inputs:** TC_CONTEXT with assessments (from Phase B), `test_cases_path` (re-read), `test_strategy_path` (re-read)\n     5|- **Outputs:** `ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md` (the primary deliverable)\n     6|- **Carries Forward:** Final metrics for audit trail\n     7|- **Flush After:** All generated spec sections, raw source content\n     8|- **Dependency:** Phase B must be COMPLETE\n     9|\n    10|---\n    11|\n    12|## Mode-Specific Behavior\n    13|\n    14|- **REPAIR:** Load the existing `ANALYSIS-SPEC-*.md` from disk.\n    15|  - Parse REPAIR_DIRECTIVES for targets matching section names or `\"global\"`.\n    16|  - If specific sections targeted → regenerate ONLY those sections. Preserve unchanged sections verbatim.\n    17|  - If `\"global\"` → regenerate the entire spec.\n    18|  - Increment version. Write to SPEC_PATH (new SESSION_ID).\n    19|- **BUILD:** Generate from scratch using template.\n    20|\n    21|---\n    22|\n    23|## Phase C Instructions\n    24|\n    25|### C.0: Mandatory Source Loading\n    26|\n    27|**CRITICAL:** After Phase B's flush, re-read what you need.\n    28|\n    29|```\n    30|READ _progress.json -> restore TC_CONTEXT with assessments\n    31|READ test_cases_path   -> TC_CONTENT (needed for original_test_cases section)\n    32|READ test_strategy_path -> STRATEGY_CONTENT (needed for traceability)\n    33|READ references/analysis-spec-template.md -> TEMPLATE (spec structure reference)\n    34|```\n    35|\n    36|**Zero Invention Checkpoint:** Verify all loaded before generating.\n    37|\n    38|### C.1: Generate ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md\n    39|\n    40|Generate the spec following the template structure. Write section by section.\n    41|\n    42|#### Spec Header (REQUIRED)\n    43|\n    44|```markdown\n    45|# {project_name} — Test Case Analysis Spec\n    46|version: {NEW_VERSION}\n    47|session: {SESSION_ID}\n    48|mode: {BUILD | REPAIR}\n    49|date: {ISO 8601}\n    50|language: {DETECTED_LANGUAGE}\n    51|sources:\n    52|  test_cases: {test_cases_path}\n    53|  test_strategy: {test_strategy_path}\n    54|  test_inventory: {automation_code_path}/test-inventory.md | N/A\n    55|spec_status: draft\n    56|```\n    57|\n    58|**WRITE** the header to SPEC_PATH immediately. Create the file.\n    59|\n    60|---\n    61|\n    62|#### Section: executive_metrics\n    63|\n    64|Summary counts derived from TC_CONTEXT:\n    65|- total_test_cases, automatable, partial, manual_only\n    66|- simple, medium, complex\n    67|- new, update, duplicate (if inventory exists)\n    68|- completeness_score (average)\n    69|- gaps_found, clarifications_needed\n    70|- status: complete\n    71|\n    72|---\n    73|\n    74|#### Section: original_test_cases\n    75|\n    76|- Capture the EXACT text from the test cases file — VERBATIM.\n    77|- Do NOT paraphrase, summarize, reword, or restructure.\n    78|- status: complete\n    79|- source: {test_cases_path}\n    80|\n    81|**APPEND** section. **FLUSH** TC_CONTENT from memory.\n    82|\n    83|---\n    84|\n    85|#### Section: quality_assessment\n    86|\n    87|Per-TC structured entries from Phase B analysis:\n    88|\n    89|```\n    90|### {TC_ID}: {title}\n    91|completeness: {score}/10\n    92|validation_points: {defined | missing}\n    93|test_data: {specified | needs_definition}\n    94|edge_cases: {yes | partial | no}\n    95|negative_scenarios: {yes | partial | no}\n    96|feasibility: {automatable | partial | manual_only}\n    97|complexity: {simple | medium | complex}\n    98|justification: {brief reason for feasibility/complexity ratings}\n    99|status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   100|source: {TC_ID} from {test_cases_path}\n   101|```\n   102|\n   103|**Source Fidelity Check:** Verify every TC ID exists in source.\n   104|\n   105|---\n   106|\n   107|#### Section: traceability_matrix\n   108|\n   109|Map test cases to strategy sections and requirements:\n   110|\n   111|```\n   112|| requirement_or_strategy_section | test_cases | coverage | status | source |\n   113|```\n   114|\n   115|**Source Fidelity Check:** Verify strategy references exist in STRATEGY_CONTENT.\n   116|Flag requirements with NO test coverage as gaps → open_questions.\n   117|\n   118|**FLUSH** STRATEGY_CONTENT from memory.\n   119|\n   120|---\n   121|\n   122|#### Section: gap_analysis\n   123|\n   124|Structured gap entries:\n   125|\n   126|```\n   127|### GAP-{NN}: {description}\n   128|type: {uncovered_requirement | missing_edge_case | missing_negative_scenario}\n   129|severity: {high | medium | low}\n   130|affected_tcs: [TC-XXX, ...]\n   131|recommendation: {suggested action}\n   132|status: complete\n   133|source: traceability analysis\n   134|```\n   135|\n   136|---\n   137|\n   138|#### Section: classification (conditional — only if INVENTORY_CONTEXT.inventory_exists)\n   139|\n   140|```\n   141|### delta_summary\n   142|new: {count}\n   143|update: {count}\n   144|duplicate: {count}\n   145|\n   146|### classification_table\n   147|| tc_id | classification | reason | existing_method | action | status | source |\n   148|```\n   149|\n   150|---\n   151|\n   152|#### Section: validations\n   153|\n   154|Results from Step 4 Quality Validation Gate:\n   155|\n   156|```\n   157|| check | result | status |\n   158||-------|--------|--------|\n   159|| V01: tc_coverage | {N}/{total} | PASS/FAIL |\n   160|| V02: classification_completeness | {N}/{total} | PASS/FAIL |\n   161|| ... | ... | ... |\n   162|```\n   163|\n   164|---\n   165|\n   166|#### Section: open_questions (ALWAYS LAST)\n   167|\n   168|Single consolidated registry:\n   169|\n   170|```\n   171|## open_questions\n   172|\n   173|### pending_inputs\n   174|| id | description | impact_level | source |\n   175|| PI-01 | ... | high/medium/low | ... |\n   176|\n   177|### coverage_gaps\n   178|| id | description | affected_area | source |\n   179|| CG-01 | ... | ... | ... |\n   180|\n   181|### assumptions_to_validate\n   182|| id | assumption | validation_method | risk_if_wrong | source |\n   183|| ASM-01 | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n   184|\n   185|### upstream_gaps_carried_forward\n   186|| id | from_artifact | description | local_coverage | source |\n   187|\n   188|### summary\n   189|total_pending_inputs: {N}\n   190|total_coverage_gaps: {N}\n   191|total_assumptions: {N}\n   192|total_upstream_gaps: {N}\n   193|analysis_status: {PROCEED | CONDITIONAL | BLOCKED}\n   194|```\n   195|\n   196|---\n   197|\n   198|### C.2: Final Spec Assembly\n   199|\n   200|1. Update spec_status in header: `complete` (if all validations pass) or `draft` (if failures)\n   201|2. Verify all sections present per template\n   202|3. Run summary count verification (stated counts vs actual items)\n   203|4. Write final SPEC_PATH to disk\n   204|\n   205|---\n   206|\n   207|## Source Fidelity Check (Final)\n   208|\n   209|Scan complete spec for:\n   210|- References to TC IDs not in source file\n   211|- Strategy references not in source documents\n   212|- Summary counts mismatched with actual table rows\n   213|- Technology-specific language (must be capability language)\n   214|- Missing status fields on any item\n   215|- Missing source tags on complete items\n   216|\n   217|IF violations → correct in place. Log corrections.\n   218|\n   219|## Post-Section Protocol\n   220|1. **Write** final ANALYSIS-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md to SPEC_PATH. Mandatory tool call.\n   221|2. **Update** _progress.json with phase C completion and final metrics.\n   222|3. **Flush** all section content from memory.\n   223|4. **Verify** SPEC_PATH exists and is non-empty.\n   224|5. **Log:** `\"Phase C complete. ANALYSIS-SPEC written. {N} sections, {gaps} gaps found.\"`\n   225|\n</file>","isError":false}}
