{"type":"tool_start","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01WCLKuZzNTrQG4GD2AUqQfL","toolName":"run_agent","args":{"action":"run","name":"","task":"Read the file /Users/andres.mesa/_dev/GLB/stepwise-fifa-qa/artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-07-e2e-suite.md in full.\n\nFor EVERY Gherkin Scenario in that file (each has a \"Test ID:\" in its Metadata block, format TC_EPIC07_XXX), produce a structured quality-assessment entry using EXACTLY this format (no prose, no extra commentary):\n\n### {TC_ID}: {short title derived from the Scenario line}\ncompleteness: {score 1-10}\nvalidation_points: {defined | missing}\ntest_data: {specified | needs_definition}\nedge_cases: {yes | partial | no}\nnegative_scenarios: {yes | partial | no}\nfeasibility: {automatable | partial | manual_only}\ncomplexity: {simple | medium | complex}\njustification: {one brief sentence justifying feasibility AND complexity, referencing step count/type}\nstatus: complete\nsource: {TC_ID} from artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-07-e2e-suite.md\n\nRules for ratings:\n- feasibility=automatable: can be fully driven via browser automation (clicks, navigation, assertions on DOM/text/state) with no manual/subjective judgment needed.\n- feasibility=partial: some steps need visual/manual verification (e.g. subjective visual regression, \"looks correct\") or external system checks not achievable via browser automation alone.\n- feasibility=manual_only: requires human judgment, physical action, or cannot be verified programmatically at all.\n- complexity=simple: single page, linear flow, <=5 steps (\"Given/When/Then/And\" lines), basic assertions.\n- complexity=medium: multi-page or conditional logic, 6-15 steps, data-driven.\n- complexity=complex: multi-system, async operations, >15 steps, state management.\n- completeness score 1-10: based on whether Given/When/Then are unambiguous and specific.\n\nDo NOT invent TC IDs. Do NOT skip any scenario. Process ALL of them — this file has 70 scenarios.\n\nAlso report: the exact count of scenarios processed, and a list of any scenario found that is missing a Test ID, Priority, or Category in its Metadata block (data-quality gaps). This epic covers responsive design/viewport testing — flag any TC requiring visual layout judgment as feasibility=partial.\n\nReturn your full output as: (1) the count of TCs processed, (2) the complete list of quality_assessment entries in the exact format above for all 70 TCs, (3) the list of any data-quality gaps found.","title":"Analyze EPIC-007 test cases","background":true,"model":"fast","modelQuery":"","limit":0,"refresh":false,"relevantFiles":["artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-07-e2e-suite.md"],"expectedOutput":"Full quality_assessment entries for all 70 TC_EPIC07_* test cases plus data-quality gap notes."}}}
