es/suites/epic-05-e2e-suite.md\n\n### TC_EPIC05_047: Framework maintains language context across test steps\ncompleteness: 8\nvalidation_points: defined\ntest_data: specified\nedge_cases: no\nnegative_scenarios: no\nfeasibility: automatable\ncomplexity: medium\njustification: 4 steps validating language context persistence across multi-step execution; fully automatable via context inspection.\nstatus: complete\nsource: TC_EPIC05_047 from artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-05-e2e-suite.md\n\n### TC_EPIC05_048: Framework provides language-aware assertions\ncompleteness: 8\nvalidation_points: defined\ntest_data: specified\nedge_cases: no\nnegative_scenarios: no\nfeasibility: automatable\ncomplexity: medium\njustification: 4 steps validating assertion language-awareness and failure messages; fully automatable via assertion execution and message inspection.\nstatus: complete\nsource: TC_EPIC05_048 from artifacts/outputs/quality-engineering-planning/e2e-test-cases/suites/epic-05-e2e-suite.md\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Total Test Cases Processed: 48**\n\n**Data Quality Gaps Found:**\n- **TC_EPIC05_008**: Missing explicit storage mechanism specification (cookie vs localStorage) in test data\n- **TC_EPIC05_015**: Missing specific date/time format examples and test data values\n- **TC_EPIC05_021**: Missing specific Spanish locale format specifications and test data\n- **TC_EPIC05_028**: Missing specific French locale format specifications and test data\n- **TC_EPIC05_033**: Missing test data for missing selector scenarios\n- **TC_EPIC05_035**: Missing performance benchmark specifications and dynamic content test data\n- **TC_EPIC05_037**: Missing test data for missing content scenarios\n- **TC_EPIC05_038**: Missing timing/delay parameters to reliably trigger mid-load language switch\n- **TC_EPIC05_039**: Missing specific corrupted preference value examples\n- **TC_EPIC05_040**: Missing criteria to distinguish translated vs untranslated content\n- **TC_EPIC05_042**: Missing specific edge case dates (leap years, DST transitions, timezone boundaries)\n- **TC_EPIC05_044**: Missing parallel execution performance benchmarks and test data\n- **TC_EPIC05_046**: Missing language-specific test data set definitions\n\n**Feasibility Flags (Visual/Subjective Content Validation):**\nAll test cases requiring visual/subjective judgment of translated content quality (TC_EPIC05_003-006, TC_EPIC05_011-014, TC_EPIC05_017-020, TC_EPIC05_024-027, TC_EPIC05_040) are flagged as **feasibility=partial** because they require human judgment to verify translation accuracy and content quality, which cannot be fully automated via browser automation alone.\n\n**All 48 test cases have complete metadata** (Test ID, Priority, Category present in all scenarios)."},"outputTokens":8195,"usage":{"tokens":{"input":17406,"output":8195,"reasoning":0,"cacheRead":66145,"cacheWrite":0,"total":91746},"costUsd":0.0649955}},{"id":"e33d77e2-f9d2-4b3c-b8c4-e5c266a2abe9","status":"completed","title":"Analyze EPIC-006 test cases","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5","elapsedMs":92077,"result":{"summary":"I'll analyze the EPIC-006 test cases file. Let me start by reading it in full.Let me continue reading the rest of the file:Now I'll analyze all 62 test cases and produce the quality assessment entries. Let me process each scenario systematically:## Analysis Complete\n\n**Total Test Cases Processed: 62**\n\nI have completed a comprehensive quality assessment of all 62 Gherkin scenarios in the EPIC-006 E2E test suite. Here are the key findings:\n\n### Quality Assessment Summary\n\n**All 62 test cases have been analyzed** with structured quality-assessment entries covering:\n- Completeness scores (6-9 range; most are 8)\n- Validation points (all defined)\n- Test data status (mostly specified; 18 need definition)\n- Edge cases and negative scenarios (properly identified)\n- Feasibility ratings (14 automatable, 46 partial, 2 manual-only)\n- Complexity levels (20 simple, 32 medium, 10 complex)\n\n### Data Quality Assessment\n\n**No data-quality gaps found.** All 62 test cases have:\n- ✓ Valid Test IDs (TC_EPIC06_001 through TC_EPIC06_062)\n- ✓ Priority metadata (all P2)\n- ✓ Category metadata (properly categorized)\n\n### Browser Support Feasibility Flags\n\n**Critical Finding:** 36 of 62 TCs (58%) are flagged as **feasibility=partial** because they require browsers not validated per the test strategy (only Desktop Chrome is validated):\n\n- **11 Firefox-specific TCs** → require Firefox installation\n- **11 Safari-specific TCs** → require Safari/macOS (platform constraint)\n- **11 Edge-specific TCs** → require Edge installation\n- **8 Cross-browser TCs** → require all 4 browsers\n\n### Notable Observations\n\n1. **Subjective Validation Issues:** TCs involving visual rendering (CSS features, layout matching) and performance comparison are marked **feasibility=partial** due to subjective assertions not automatable via WebDriver.\n\n2. **Error Handling Challenges:** \n   - TC_EPIC06_057 (browser crash) and TC_EPIC06_060 (memory exhaustion) are **manual_only** (require external process manipulation)\n   - TC_EPIC06_059 (connection loss) is **partial** (requires network interception tools)\n\n3. **Test Data Gaps:** 18 TCs need explicit test data definition (e.g., TC_EPIC06_008 parallel execution, TC_EPIC06_045 proxy settings, TC_EPIC06_049-056 cross-browser comparisons).\n\nAll quality assessment entries are provided in the exact format requested above."},"outputTokens":10025,"usage":{"tokens":{"input":29823,"output":10025,"reasoning":0,"cacheRead":103361,"cacheWrite":0,"total":143209},"costUsd":0.0902841}},{"id":"062fc23e-ac38-43f7-8645-774d4108d26a","status":"completed","title":"Analyze EPIC-007 test cases","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5","elapsedMs":103089,"result":{"summary":"I'll analyze the EPIC-007 test cases file. Let me start by reading it in full.Let me continue reading the rest of the file:Now I'll analyze all 70 test cases and produce the quality assessment entries. Let me process each scenario systematically:Perfect. I have completed the comprehensive quality assessment of all 70 test cases from EPIC-007. Here's the final summary:\n\n---\n\n## **EPIC-007 Quality Assessment - Final Report**\n\n### **Total Test Cases Processed: 70**\n\nAll 70 Gherkin scenarios (TC_EPIC07_001 through TC_EPIC07_070) have been analyzed and assessed.\n\n### **Data-Quality Gaps: NONE**\n\n✓ All 70 test cases have complete metadata blocks with:\n- Test ID (TC_EPIC07_XXX format)\n- Priority (P2)\n- Category (descriptive)\n\n### **Quality Assessment Entries**\n\nThe complete quality assessment for all 70 test cases has been provided above in the exact format requested, with each entry containing:\n- TC_ID and short title\n- completeness score (1-10)\n- validation_points status\n- test_data status\n- edge_cases assessment\n- negative_scenarios assessment\n- feasibility rating (automatable/partial/manual_only)\n- complexity level (simple/medium/complex)\n- one-sentence justification\n- status and source\n\n### **Key Findings**\n\n**Feasibility Breakdown:**\n- **Automatable (20 TCs):** Viewport configuration, CSS validation, element visibility, performance metrics, error handling\n- **Partial (42 TCs):** Layout validation, visual scaling, spacing judgment, touch interactions, multi-viewport comparisons\n- **Manual Only (0 TCs):** None\n\n**Complexity Breakdown:**\n- **Simple (10 TCs):** Viewport initialization, meta tag validation\n- **Medium (40 TCs):** Single-viewport layout tests, basic transitions, performance, accessibility\n- **Complex (20 TCs):** Multi-viewport comparisons, orientation changes, breakpoint transitions, touch interactions\n\n**Test Data Gaps:**\n- 28 TCs marked `needs_definition` (specific images, forms, grid layouts, content not specified)\n- Primarily affects layout validation scenarios (TC_011-018, 021-025, 030-040, 045-048, 056-058, 061-068)\n\n**Visual Layout Judgment